{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.MassElementNf","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.MassElementNf","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonical","kind":"instance","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.lean#L64-L77","doc":"**Unit-coefficient skeleton instance.**  Sets each NF channel\ncoefficient `(a₁, a₃, a₅) = (1, 1, 1)`; positivity closes by\n`norm_num`.  Encodes none of the actual NF-decomposition content\n(the genuine coefficients are q-rational functions of the braid\nword) but discharges the §3b-cond hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.a₅_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.a₅_pos","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.a₃_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.a₃_pos","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.a₁_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.a₁_pos","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.lean#L60-L60","doc":"All NF coefficients are positive for massive particles. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.gamma_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.gamma_zero","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.lean#L58-L58","doc":"The γ coefficient vanishes (photon masslessness). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.a₅","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.a₅","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.lean#L56-L56","doc":"NF coefficient for the e⁻ channel (degree 3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.a₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.a₃","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.lean#L54-L54","doc":"NF coefficient for the L₊ + L₋ channel (degree 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.a₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.a₁","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.lean#L52-L52","doc":"NF coefficient for the σ₀ + σ₁ channel (degree 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF.mk","kind":"ctor","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeMassNF","kind":"class","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.lean#L43-L62","doc":"**HeckeMassNF** — the conjectural class.\n\nAn instance for braid data `β` asserts that the Hecke mass element\ndecomposes in the NF basis with vanishing $\\gamma$ coefficient and\npositive coefficients $a_1, a_3, a_5 > 0$. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:mass-element-nf","label":"prop:mass-element-nf","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassNFBasis.eMinus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassNFBasis.eMinus","kind":"ctor","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassNFBasis.LpLm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassNFBasis.LpLm","kind":"ctor","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassNFBasis.sigma01","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassNFBasis.sigma01","kind":"ctor","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassNFBasis.gamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassNFBasis.gamma","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MassNFBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MassNFBasis","kind":"inductive","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-element-nf.lean#L35-L41","doc":"Enumeration of the four NF basis elements of $H_3(R, q)$\nrelevant to the mass element decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}